2026-03-07T17:49:36.894Z [DEBUG] Tool invocation result: {"total_count":16,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"id":4038472418,"number":194,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"ci: configure trivial jobs to use ubuntu-slim runner","body":"## Description\n\nSwitch workflow jobs that only require pre-installed tooling to `ubuntu-slim`, reducing cost and infrastructure burden. Jobs requiring packages absent from ubuntu-slim (e.g. `dejagnu`, `bison`, `cmake`, `gcc-arm-none-eabi`, `libgmp-dev`) remain on `ubuntu-latest`. Also adds the missing `permissions: {}` at the workflow level in `copilot-setup-steps.yml` for consistency with the rest of the repo's CI conventions.\n\n**→ `ubuntu-slim`** (no extra apt installs needed):\n- `commitlint.yml` — `commitlint` (git + npm only)\n- `shell-unit-tests.yml` — all three jobs (bash scripts only)\n- `libiberty-tests.yml` — all three jobs (gcc + make, both pre-installed)\n- `build-toolchain.yml` — `check-changes`, `build-status`\n- `binutils-tests.yml` — `check-changes`, `binutils-tests-status`\n- `gcc-selftests.yml` — `check-changes`, `gcc-selftests-status`\n- `gdb-selftests.yml` — `check-changes`, `gdb-selftests-status`\n- `copilot-setup-steps.yml` — `copilot-setup-steps` (git + gh-aw action)\n\n**Kept on `ubuntu-latest`** (require packages not in ubuntu-slim):\n- `binutils-tests` — needs `dejagnu`, `gcc-arm-none-eabi`\n- `gcc-selftests` — needs `bison`, `libgmp-dev`, `libmpfr-dev`, `libmpc-dev`\n- `gdb-selftests` — needs `bison`, `libgmp-dev`, `libmpfr-dev`, `libreadline-dev`\n- `build` (build-toolchain) — needs `cmake`, `gcc-arm-none-eabi`, `gdb-multiarch`, `openocd`, etc.\n\nAll `*.lock.yml` files excluded per issue criteria (auto-generated).\n\n## Testing\n\nChanges are YAML-only runner label and permissions updates. Validated by cross-referencing each job's tool usage against the [ubuntu-slim pre-installed package list](https://github.com/actions/runner-images/blob/main/images/ubuntu-slim/ubuntu-slim-Readme.md).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] The PR title follows the Conventional Commits format (see note below)\n- [x] Changes are documented where appropriate\n\n---\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **PR title must follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) format.**\n>\n> PRs are squashed into the target branch using the **PR title** as the commit message.\n> The PR title must therefore conform to commitlint requirements:\n>\n> ```\n> <type>[(optional scope)][!]: <description>\n> ```\n>\n> Common types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `chore`, `refactor`, `test`, `ci`, `build`, `perf`, `style`, `revert`\n>\n> Examples: `feat: add ARMv8-M support`, `fix: correct stack calculation`, `docs: update build instructions`\n>\n> Individual commits **within** the PR do **not** need to follow this format.\n\n<!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT -->\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Original prompt</summary>\n\n> \n> ----\n> \n> *This section details on the original issue you should resolve*\n> \n> <issue_title>ci: Configure trivial jobs to use the `ubuntu-slim` runner</issue_title>\n> <issue_description>## Problem Statement\n> \n> To minimise workflow burden on GitHub's infrastructure evaluate all workflow jobs and, if they meet the following criteria, change their configured runner to `ubuntu-slim`.\n> \n> - **Only** uses / needs tools listed as available [here](https://github.com/actions/runner-images/blob/main/images/ubuntu-slim/ubuntu-slim-Readme.md)\n> - Is not a `.github/workflows/**.lock.yml` file\n> \n> `ubuntu-slim` is cheaper per minute and less burden on GitHub's infrastructure.\n> \n> ---\n> \n> > **Note:** If this issue leads to a pull request, the **PR title** must follow\n> > [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) format, as required by this\n> > repository's commitlint configuration (e.g. `feat: add support for Cortex-M55`).\n> </issue_description>\n> \n> ## Comments on the Issue (you are @copilot in this section)\n> \n> <comments>\n> </comments>\n> \n\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX -->\n\n- Fixes grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32#193\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS -->\n---\n\n🔒 GitHub Advanced Security automatically protects Copilot coding agent pull requests. You can protect all pull requests by enabling Advanced Security for your repositories. [Learn more about Advanced Security.](https://gh.io/cca-advanced-security)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","user":{"login":"Copilot","id":198982749,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","site_admin":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions"},"comments":2,"closed_at":"2026-03-07T17:15:07Z","created_at":"2026-03-07T13:19:45Z","updated_at":"2026-03-07T17:15:08Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/194","html_url":"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/194","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/194/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/194/events","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/194/labels{/name}","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32","pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pulls/194","html_url":"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/194","diff_url":"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/194.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/194.patch","merged_at":"2026-03-07T17:15:07Z"},"reactions":{"total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/194/reactions"},"assignees":[{"login":"Copilot","id":198982749,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","site_admin":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions"},{"login":"grahame-white","id":214149191,"node_id":"U_kgDODMOoRw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214149191?v=4","html_url":"https://github.com/grahame-white","gravatar_id":"","type":"User","site_admin":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/events{/privacy}","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/following{/other_user}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/followers","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/gists{/gist_id}","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/repos","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/subscriptions"}],"node_id":"PR_kwDORdWri87IuCDm","draft":false},{"id":4038300849,"number":190,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"ci: fix push_repo_memory spawnSync ENOBUFS on large repo","body":"## Description\n\n`push_repo_memory` was failing with `spawnSync git ENOBUFS` when the `memory/audit-workflows` branch didn't yet exist. The internal `push_repo_memory.cjs` script took the orphan-branch path: `git checkout --orphan` followed by `git rm -rf .` — on this repo's ~217k-file working tree, that command's output overflows Node.js's `spawnSync` 1 MB buffer.\n\n**Fix:** Add an \"Ensure memory branch exists\" step in the `push_repo_memory` job in `audit-workflows.lock.yml`, before the push step, that pre-creates `memory/audit-workflows` via the GitHub REST API when it doesn't exist:\n\n1. `POST /git/trees` — tree with a single `.gitkeep` file (`{\"tree\":[{\"path\":\".gitkeep\",\"mode\":\"100644\",\"type\":\"blob\",\"content\":\"\"}]}`)\n2. `POST /git/commits` — root commit, no parents\n3. `POST /git/refs` — create `refs/heads/memory/audit-workflows`\n\nThis forces `push_repo_memory.cjs` to always take the existing-branch path (fetch → checkout → diff → push), bypassing the orphan creation entirely.\n\n**Note on tree creation:** The GitHub REST API rejects an empty tree `{\"tree\":[]}` with HTTP 422 \"Invalid tree info\". The tree must contain at least one entry, so a single empty `.gitkeep` file is used.\n\n**Why the fix is in `audit-workflows.lock.yml` rather than the `.md` source:** gh-aw v0.53.6 provides no frontmatter mechanism to inject steps into the auto-generated `push_repo_memory` job. All alternatives were verified and blocked:\n- `steps:` / `post-steps:` inject into the agent job, which cannot have `contents: write` (blocked by gh-aw's security enforcement even with `strict: false`)\n- `safe-outputs: steps:` injects only into the `safe_outputs` job, not `push_repo_memory`\n- `jobs:` custom entries cannot override auto-generated jobs (error: \"job already exists\") and are not added to `push_repo_memory`'s `needs:` automatically\n\nThe lock.yml edit is accompanied by a detailed `# INTENTIONAL MANUAL EDIT` comment explaining the constraint and when re-application is needed. The `audit-workflows.md` \"Large-Repository Compatibility\" section and `.github/copilot-instructions.md` are updated to document this intentional exception.\n\n**Note:** Once the `memory/audit-workflows` branch exists after the first successful run, subsequent runs — including runs from a freshly compiled lock.yml — will work without this step. The step only needs to be re-applied if `gh aw compile` is run while the branch doesn't exist.\n\n## Testing\n\nValidated YAML syntax with `python3 -c \"import yaml; yaml.safe_load(...)\"`. The step is idempotent — if the branch already exists, it logs and skips. All gh-aw frontmatter alternatives were compiled and tested to confirm they are not viable. The initial fix was tested against a live CI run (run 22798555427) which revealed the empty-tree HTTP 422 error; the corrected tree payload was confirmed to be the appropriate fix.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] The PR title follows the Conventional Commits format (see note below)\n- [x] Changes are documented where appropriate\n\n<!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT -->\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Original prompt</summary>\n\n> \n> ----\n> \n> *This section details on the original issue you should resolve*\n> \n> <issue_title>[aw] Agentic Workflow Audit Agent failed</issue_title>\n> <issue_description>### Workflow Failure\n> \n> **Workflow:** [Agentic Workflow Audit Agent](https://github.com/github/gh-aw/tree/852cb06ad52958b402ed982b69957ffc57ca0619/.github/workflows/audit-workflows.md)  \n> **Branch:** 13.3.rel1  \n> **Run:** https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22783839711\n> \n> \n> **⚠️ Repo-Memory Push Failed**: The push-repo-memory job failed to write memory back to the repository. This may indicate a permission issue, a configuration error, or a network problem. Check the [workflow run](https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22783839711) for details.\n> \n> \n> \n> ### Action Required\n> \n> **Option 1: Assign this issue to Copilot**\n> \n> Assign this issue to Copilot using the `agentic-workflows` sub-agent to automatically debug and fix the workflow failure.\n> \n> **Option 2: Manually invoke the agent**\n> \n> Debug this workflow failure using your favorite Agent CLI and the `agentic-workflows` prompt.\n> \n> - Start your agent\n> - Load the `agentic-workflows` prompt from `.github/agents/agentic-workflows.agent.md` or <https://github.com/github/gh-aw/blob/main/.github/agents/agentic-workflows.agent.md>\n> - Type `debug the agentic workflow audit-workflows failure in https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22783839711`\n> \n> \n> > Generated from [Agentic Workflow Audit Agent](https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22783839711)\n> > - [x] expires <!-- gh-aw-expires: 2026-03-13T22:12:07.946Z --> on Mar 13, 2026, 10:12 PM UTC\n> \n> <!-- gh-aw-agentic-workflow: Agentic Workflow Audit Agent, gh-aw-tracker-id: audit-workflows-daily, id: 22783839711, workflow_id: audit-workflows, run: https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22783839711 --></issue_description>\n> \n> ## Comments on the Issue (you are @copilot in this section)\n> \n> <comments>\n> </comments>\n> \n\n\n</details>\n\n\n> **Custom agent used: agentic-workflows**\n> GitHub Agentic Workflows (gh-aw) - Create, debug, and upgrade AI-powered workflows with intelligent prompt routing\n\n\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX -->\n\n- Fixes grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32#189\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS -->\n---\n\n🔒 GitHub Advanced Security automatically protects Copilot coding agent pull requests. You can protect all pull requests by enabling Advanced Security for your repositories. [Learn more about Advanced Security.](https://gh.io/cca-advanced-security)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","user":{"login":"Copilot","id":198982749,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","site_admin":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions"},"comments":4,"closed_at":"2026-03-07T17:41:18Z","created_at":"2026-03-07T11:45:19Z","updated_at":"2026-03-07T17:41:19Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/190","html_url":"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/190","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/190/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/190/events","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/190/labels{/name}","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32","pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pulls/190","html_url":"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/190","diff_url":"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/190.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/190.patch","merged_at":"2026-03-07T17:41:18Z"},"reactions":{"total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/190/reactions"},"assignees":[{"login":"Copilot","id":198982749,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","site_admin":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions"},{"login":"grahame-white","id":214149191,"node_id":"U_kgDODMOoRw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214149191?v=4","html_url":"https://github.com/grahame-white","gravatar_id":"","type":"User","site_admin":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/events{/privacy}","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/following{/other_user}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/followers","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/gists{/gist_id}","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/repos","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/subscriptions"}],"node_id":"PR_kwDORdWri87ItfiL","draft":false},{"id":4038287891,"number":188,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix: increase daily-test-improver repo-memory max-file-size to 10 MiB","body":"## Description\n\nThe Daily Test Improver `push_repo_memory` job was failing because `build-common.sh` (12 KiB) exceeded the default 10 KiB per-file size limit, causing the entire memory write to abort.\n\n- **`daily-test-improver.md`**: Replace `repo-memory: true` with explicit `max-file-size: 102400` (100 KiB), matching the limit already used by `audit-workflows.md`\n- **`daily-test-improver.lock.yml`**: Update `MAX_FILE_SIZE` and `MAX_PATCH_SIZE` from `10240` → `102400` to match\n- **`daily-test-improver.lock.yml`**: Update `GH_AW_MEMORY_CONSTRAINTS` string to advertise the actual configured limits (`102400 bytes / 100 KiB`), replacing the stale `10240 bytes` values that no longer matched\n\n## Testing\n\nValidated against the failing run ([#22793310237](https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22793310237)) — error was `build-common.sh (12066 bytes > 10240 bytes)`, which the increased limit resolves.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] The PR title follows the Conventional Commits format (see note below)\n- [x] Changes are documented where appropriate\n\n<!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT -->\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Original prompt</summary>\n\n> \n> ----\n> \n> *This section details on the original issue you should resolve*\n> \n> <issue_title>[aw] Daily Test Improver fa