ite/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/repos","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/subscriptions"}],"node_id":"PR_kwDORdWri87IkkJz","draft":false},{"id":4035353146,"number":173,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"ci: update agentic workflows to align with gnu-tools-for-stm32 repository","body":"The agentic workflow `.md` files were imported from generic templates containing instructions for Go, JavaScript, Python, and .NET projects — none of which apply here. Instructions are now written in terms of repository patterns rather than specific file names, so they stay accurate as the codebase evolves.\n\n## Description\n\n- **`code-simplifier.md`** — Replace four language-specific standards blocks (Go/JS/Python/.NET) with shell script and CI YAML conventions matching this repo. Validation commands now use the `tests/` discovery pattern (`for t in tests/test-*.sh`) and `bash -n` syntax checking.\n\n- **`daily-test-improver.md`** — Drop irrelevant network allowances (`dotnet`, `node`, `python`, `rust`, `java`). Task 1 cross-reference updated to describe patterns (CI workflow files in `.github/workflows/`, build scripts in repo root) rather than specific filenames.\n\n- **`plan.md`** — Remove the `cookie` label (template artefact). Fix `.github/instructions/*.instructions.md` reference (path doesn't exist) to point at `.github/copilot-instructions.md`. Fix stale inline comment: `max: 50` now correctly reads `# Maximum 50 sub-issues per group`.\n\n- **`shared/ci-optimization-strategies.md`** — Replace Go-specific `go test` analysis with the actual patterns of this repo: Phase 1 describes the three-job CI structure (`check-changes` → main → `<name>-status`), qualified to \"most test/build workflows\" with `commitlint.yml` noted as an intentional exception; Phase 2 describes cross-referencing `tests/test-*.sh` scripts against all workflow YAML files; Phase 3B reflects the `$(nproc)` build parallelism pattern. Restored \"Matrix strategy effectiveness\" as an explicit analysis bullet.\n\n## Testing\n\nDocumentation-only changes. Verified no specific file names remain hardcoded across all modified files. Verified factual accuracy of CI pattern claims against actual workflow files (e.g., confirmed `commitlint.yml` is a single-job workflow without the three-job pattern).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] The PR title follows the Conventional Commits format (see note below)\n- [x] Changes are documented where appropriate\n\n<!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT -->\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Original prompt</summary>\n\n> \n> ----\n> \n> *This section details on the original issue you should resolve*\n> \n> <issue_title>Review agentic workflows and bring in line with this repository</issue_title>\n> <issue_description>## Brief\n> \n> The agentic workflows `.github/workflows/**.md` were imported from default templates and not all of the instructions are appropriate for this specific repository and its contents.\n> \n> ## Acceptance Criteria\n> \n> **CRITICAL** Do not change the intent of the agentic workflows.\n> \n> - Workflows brought in line with the specific needs of this repository\n> - Do not modify the `.github/workflows/**.yml` files</issue_description>\n> \n> ## Comments on the Issue (you are @copilot in this section)\n> \n> <comments>\n> </comments>\n> \n\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX -->\n\n- Fixes grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#172\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS -->\n---\n\n💬 We'd love your input! Share your thoughts on Copilot coding agent in our [2 minute survey](https://gh.io/copilot-coding-agent-survey).\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","user":{"login":"Copilot","id":198982749,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4","