n":"Copilot","id":198982749,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","site_admin":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions"},{"login":"grahame-white","id":214149191,"node_id":"U_kgDODMOoRw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214149191?v=4","html_url":"https://github.com/grahame-white","gravatar_id":"","type":"User","site_admin":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/events{/privacy}","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/following{/other_user}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/followers","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/gists{/gist_id}","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/repos","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/subscriptions"}],"node_id":"PR_kwDORdWri87Ij3Vs","draft":false},{"id":4032862449,"number":161,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat: add gcc-first stage cache restore/build/save triple with dedicated build script","body":"## Description\n\nAdds a `restore → build → save` cache triple for the `gcc-first` (III-1) stage to `build-toolchain.yml`, following the identical pattern already used for `binutils`. This is the first incremental step toward per-stage caching (issue #142), deliberately split so `gcc-first` and `newlib` can be validated independently.\n\n**Changes:**\n- **Restore cache – gcc-first**: Unconditional restore keyed on `steps.stage-hashes.outputs['gcc-first']` (bracket notation required for hyphenated output names; same `stage-v1-` prefix convention as binutils)\n- **Build stage – gcc-first**: Gated on both `cache-gcc-first` and `cache-toolchain` not being hits; calls `./build-gcc-first.sh` directly (see below)\n- **Save cache – gcc-first**: Same condition as build; captures cumulative `install-native` state through gcc-first\n\n- **`build-gcc-first.sh` (new)**: Standalone script containing only the gcc-first (III-1) build logic, extracted from `build-toolchain.sh` so that changes to other parts of the toolchain build do not invalidate the gcc-first stage cache. Accepts the same `--build_type` and `--skip_steps` flags as `build-toolchain.sh`; `--skip_stages` is accepted but ignored. Uses `cd \"$script_path\"` before sourcing `build-common.sh` to ensure `ROOT=$(pwd)` always resolves to the repo root. Does **not** wipe `install-native` — binutils output must already be present.\n- **`build-toolchain.sh` – delegate gcc-first**: Inline gcc-first build block (~40 lines) replaced with `\"$script_path/build-gcc-first.sh\" \"$@\"` when the stage is not skipped.\n- **`build-toolchain.yml` – stage hash isolation**: Added `gcc_first_scripts_hash` derived from `build-gcc-first.sh + build-toolchain-args.sh + build-common.sh`; `key_gcc_first` now uses `gcc_first_scripts_hash` so changes to `build-toolchain.sh` that don't touch `build-gcc-first.sh` or `build-toolchain-args.sh` no longer invalidate the gcc-first cache. `build-toolchain-args.sh` is included because `build-gcc-first.sh` sources it, so args parser changes could alter gcc-first behavior. Added `build-gcc-first.sh` to paths-filter.\n- **`shell-unit-tests.yml`**: Added `build-gcc-first.sh` to paths-filter so unit tests run when the new script changes.\n- **`build-toolchain.sh` fix 1 – preserve install-native on partial builds**: Guard `rm -rf $INSTALLDIR_NATIVE` at startup with `if [ \"x$skip_stages\" == \"x\" ]`. When `--skip_stages` is used (incremental partial build), `install-native` is no longer wiped at script startup, so restored predecessor-stage cache content (e.g., `arm-none-eabi/bin/` from the binutils cache restore) is preserved for the partial build. Full builds (no `--skip_stages`) continue to wipe `install-native` as before.\n- **`build-toolchain.sh` fix 2 – skip III-11 specs on partial builds**: Guard the III-11 `specs` post-build step with `stage_is_skipped \"gcc-final\"`. The specs step enumerates multilib directories via `arm-none-eabi-gcc -print-multi-lib` and copies spec files into them, but those directories (e.g., `arm-none-eabi/lib/arm/v5te/softfp/`) are only created by `newlib`/`gcc-final`. When `gcc-final` is being skipped, the specs step now skips with a clear message instead of failing with `cp: No such file or directory`.\n\nThe three workflow steps are inserted after `Save cache – binutils` and before `Cache toolchain build`. When `src/gcc/` changes but `src/binutils/` is unchanged, the binutils cache hits and only gcc-first rebuilds.\n\n**Root cause of `build-toolchain.sh` fix 1:** Without the guard, `Build stage – gcc-first` would run with `--skip_stages=binutils,...`, which wiped `install-native` (destroying the just-restored binutils cache), then skipped binutils (so `arm-none-eabi/bin/` was never repopulated), then the post-build III-9 `strip_host_objects` step ran `find install-native/arm-none-eabi/bin/` which exited 1 under `set -e`.\n\n**Root cause of `build-toolchain.sh` fix 2:** After fix 1, the III-11 `specs` step was still reached. Its existing guard (`[ -x arm-none-eabi-gcc ]`) passes after gcc-first builds, but the multilib directories that `cp` targets only exist after `newlib` runs. Per `docs/build-stages.md`, specs depends on `gcc-final`; guarding with `stage_is_skipped \"gcc-final\"` correctly skips specs for any partial build that has not yet run gcc-final.\n\n**Note:** Because `build-gcc-first.sh` and `gcc_first_scripts_hash` inputs changed, the gcc-first stage cache is invalidated on the next CI run. Subsequent runs where only `build-toolchain.sh` changes (but not `build-gcc-first.sh` or `build-toolchain-args.sh`) will no longer invalidate the gcc-first cache.\n\n## Testing\n\n- YAML validated syntactically via Python `yaml.safe_load`\n- `--skip_stages` values verified against the validation whitelist in `build-toolchain.sh` (`binutils|gcc-first|newlib|newlib-nano|gcc-final|gcc-size-libstdcxx|gdb`)\n- Both shell unit test suites pass (95 tests total: 36 in `test-build-common.sh` + 59 in `test-build-toolchain-args.sh`) after all `build-toolchain.sh` changes\n- CodeQL analysis: 0 alerts\n- Both CI failures reproduced and root causes confirmed via GitHub Actions job logs\n- Confirmed `build-gcc-first.sh` sources `build-toolchain-args.sh` (line 59), validating inclusion in `gcc_first_scripts_hash`\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] The PR title follows the Conventional Commits format (see note below)\n- [x] Changes are documented where appropriate\n\n<!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT -->\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Original prompt</summary>\n\n\n----\n\n*This section details on the original issue you should resolve*\n\n<issue_title>[plan] Add gcc-first stage cache restore/build/save triple to build-toolchain.yml</issue_title>\n<issue_description>## Objective\n\nAdd a `restore → build → save` cache triple for the **`gcc-first`** (III-1) build stage in `.github/workflows/build-toolchain.yml`, following the same pattern already used for the `binutils` stage.\n\n## Context\n\nThis is the first of two incremental steps to implement issue grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#142. The change has been deliberately split so that `gcc-first` and `newlib` can be validated independently — implementing both at once previously made debugging too difficult.\n\nThe `Compute stage source hashes` step already emits a `gcc-first` key via `steps.stage-hashes.outputs.gcc-first`. The `stage_is_skipped` logic in `build-toolchain.sh` supports `--skip_stages=binutils,...` to run only the `gcc-first` stage when its predecessors' outputs are already present in `install-native`.\n\n## Files to Modify\n\n- `.github/workflows/build-toolchain.yml`\n\n## Approach\n\nInsert the following three steps **after** the `Save cache – binutils` step and **before** the `Cache toolchain build` step:\n\n```yaml\n# --- Stage: gcc-first ---\n- name: Restore cache – gcc-first\n  id: cache-gcc-first\n  uses: actions/cache/restore@cdf6c1fa76f9f475f3d7449005a359c84ca0f306 # v5.0.3\n  with:\n    path: install-native\n    key: ${{ runner.os }}-stage-v1-${{ steps.stage-hashes.outputs.gcc-first }}\n\n- name: Build stage – gcc-first\n  if: steps.cache-gcc-first.outputs.cache-hit != 'true' && steps.cache-toolchain.outputs.cache-hit != 'true'\n  run: |\n    export JOBS=$(nproc)\n    ./build-toolchain.sh \\\n      --skip_steps=mingw,mingw-gdb-with-python,gdb-with-python,manual,package_sources \\\n      --skip_stages=binutils,newlib,newlib-nano,gcc-final,gcc-size-libstdcxx,gdb\n\n- name: Save cache – gcc-first\n  if: steps.cache-gcc-first.outputs.cache-hit != 'true' && steps.cache-toolchain.outputs.cache-hit != 'true'\n  uses: actions/cache/save@cdf6c1fa76f9f475f3d7449005a359c84ca0f306 # v5.0.3\n  with:\n    path: install-native\n    key: ${{ runner.os }}-stage-v1-${{ steps.stage-hashes.outputs.gcc-first }}\n```\n\n**Key implementation notes:**\n\n- Use the same actions/cache SHA already present in the workflow (`cdf6c1fa76f9f475f3d7449005a359c84ca0f306 # v5.0.3`).\n- The `--skip_stages=binutils,...` argument tells `build-toolchain.sh` to skip the binutils stage and run only `gcc-first`. The binutils output must already be present in `install-native` (from the binutils cache triple that precedes this block).\n- `steps.cache-toolchain.outputs.cache-hit` is referenced before the `Cache toolchain build` step runs, so it evaluates to `''` at this point (which satisfies `!= 'true'`). This matches the same pattern already used in the binutils build/save steps. The condition will short-circuit properly if the monolithic cache later replaces this with a hit on a future run.\n- The `cache-gcc-first` restore has no `if:` guard (unconditional restore), ensuring that a previously-cached `gcc-first` snapshot (which includes cumulative `install-native` state from binutils through gcc-first) is always preferred over rebuilding. The restore action is a no-op if the key is not found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The three new steps appear in the correct position in `build-toolchain.yml` (after `Save cache – binutils`, before `Cache toolchain build`)\n- [ ] The cache key uses `stage-v1-` prefix and `steps.stage-hashes.outputs.gcc-first`\n- [ ] The build step skips `binutils` (already done) and all stages after `gcc-first`\n- [ ] The build and save steps share the same `if:` condition\n- [ ] When `src/gcc/` changes but `src/binutils/` is unchanged: binutils cache hits, gcc-first miss triggers a build, save captures the new gcc-first state\n- [ ] YAML is valid and the workflow lints cleanly\n- [ ] The existing `binutils` cache triple is not modified\nRelated to grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#142\n\n\n\n\n> Generated by [Plan Command](https://github.com/grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22754576747) for issue grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#142 · [◷](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Agrahame-white%2Fgnu-tools-for-stm32+is%3Aissue+%22gh-aw-workflow-call-id%3A+grahame-white%2Fgnu-tools-for-stm32%2Fplan%22+in%3Abody)\n>\n> To install this [agentic workflow](https://github.com/github/gh-aw/tree/852cb06ad52958b402ed982b69957ffc57ca0619/.github/workflows/plan.md), run\n> ```\n> gh aw add github/gh-aw/.github/workflows/plan.md@852cb06ad52958b402ed982b69957ffc57ca0619\n> ```\n> - [x] expires <!-- gh-aw-expires: 2026-03-08T08:07:28.690Z --> on Mar 8, 2026, 8:07 AM UTC\n\n<!-- gh-aw-agentic-workflow: Plan Command, engine: copilot, id: 22754576747, workflow_id: plan, run: https://github.com/grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22754576747 -->\n\n<!-- gh-aw-workflow-id: plan -->\n<!-- gh-aw-workflow-call-id: grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/plan --></issue_description>\n\n## Comments ...\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX -->\n\n- Fixes grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#159\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS -->\n---\n\n💬 We'd love your input! Share your thoughts on Copilot coding agent in our [2 minute survey](https://gh.io/copilot-coding-agent-survey).\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","user":{"login":"Copilot","id":198982749,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","site_admin":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions"},"comments":8,"closed_at":"2026-03-07T16:38:24Z","created_at":"2026-03-06T08:08:21Z","updated_at":"2026-03-07T16:38:26Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/161","html_url":"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/161","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/161/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/161/events","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/161/labels{/name}","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32","pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pulls/161","html_url":"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/161","diff_url":"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/161.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/161.patch","merged_at":"2026-03-07T16:38:24Z"},"reactions":{"total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/161/reactions"},"assignees":[{"login":"Copilot","id":198982749,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","site_admin":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions"},{"login":"grahame-white","id":214149191,"node_id":"U_kgDODMOoRw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214149191?v=4","html_url":"https://github.com/grahame-white","gravatar_id":"","type":"User","site_admin":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/events{/privacy}","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/following{/other_user}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/followers","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/gists{/gist_id}","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/repos","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/subscriptions"}],"node_id":"PR_kwDORdWri87IbqNO","draft":false},{"id":4032854468,"number":158,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"ci: fix CI Optimization Coach prompt for this shell/C toolchain project","body":"## Description\n\n`ci-coach.md` imported `shared/ci-data-analysis.md`, a module designed for the `gh-aw` Go/Node.js project. The compiled lock file injected incompatible setup steps that failed before the agent could start:\n\n- `Setup Node.js` with `cache-dependency-path: actions/setup/js/package-lock.json` — path doesn't exist → fatal npm cache error, all subsequent steps skipped\n- `Setup Go` with `go-version-file: go.mod` — no `go.mod` here\n- `make deps-dev/lint/build/recompile` — no `Makefile`\n- `npm ci` in `./actions/setup/js` — directory doesn't exist\n- Download runs for `ci.yml` — no such workflow in this repo\n\n**`ci-coach.md` fixes** (lock file must be regenerated via `gh aw compile` after merge):\n\n- **Remove `shared/ci-data-analysis.md` import** — eliminates all Go/npm setup steps on next compilation\n- **Target workflows**: replace `ci.yml` with the six actual workflows (`build-toolchain.yml`, `binutils-tests.yml`, `gcc-selftests.yml`, `gdb-selftests.yml`, `libiberty-tests.yml`, `shell-unit-tests.yml`)\n- **Data access**: replace stale pre-downloaded file references (`/tmp/ci-runs.json`, `/tmp/ci-artifacts/`, etc.) with instructions to use live GitHub MCP tools\n- **Project context**: add explicit note that this is a shell/C toolchain — no `go.mod`, `Makefile`, or `actions/setup/js/`\n- **Phase 2**: rewrite test-coverage analysis for this repo's actual test structure (shell + DejaGnu + selftests)\n- **Phase 3**: remove fuzz-test optimisation items (no fuzz tests here)\n- **Phase 5**: replace `make lint && make build && make test-unit && make recompile` with `bash tests/test-build-common.sh`; fix cache-memory path to `/tmp/gh-aw/cache-memory/`\n- **Duplicates**: remove duplicated `## Data Available` and `### Phase 5` section headers\n- **PR template example**: replace Go-specific `go test` restructuring example with a cache-key optimisation example relevant to this repo\n\n> ⚠️ `ci-coach.lock.yml` is auto-generated and must not be edited directly. Run `gh aw compile` (or trigger **Agentic Maintenance** → `upgrade`) after merging to regenerate the lock file from the corrected source.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Verified `bash tests/test-build-common.sh` passes (28/28).\n- Confirmed no remaining references to `ci.yml`, `make lint/build/test-unit/recompile`, `go.mod`, `go test`, `*_test.go`, `ci-data-analysis`, or stale `/tmp/ci-*` paths.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] The PR title follows the Conventional Commits format (see note below)\n- [x] Changes are documented where appropriate\n\n> [!WARNING]\n>\n> <details>\n> <summary>Firewall rules blocked me from connecting to one or more addresses (expand for details)</summary>\n>\n> #### I tried to connect to the following addresses, but was blocked by firewall rules:\n>\n> - `ht