nt drops from 2 → 1, content intact\n- Add `trap 'rm -rf \"$_BHL_TMPDIR\"' EXIT` immediately after `mktemp -d` to ensure the temp directory is always cleaned up, even if `set -e` aborts the script early\n- Wrap the bare `break_hardlink` invocation in the hard-link test with `assert_zero_exit` so failures are recorded as test failures rather than aborting the harness\n\nSubshell wrappers (`bash -c`) are used for error-path tests to prevent `error()`'s `exit 1` from aborting the test script.\n\n## Testing\n\n`bash tests/test-build-common.sh` — 36 passed, 0 failed (28 pre-existing + 8 new).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] The PR title follows the Conventional Commits format (see note below)\n- [x] Changes are documented where appropriate\n\n<!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT -->\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Original prompt</summary>\n\n> \n> ----\n> \n> *This section details on the original issue you should resolve*\n> \n> <issue_title>[aw] Daily Test Improver failed</issue_title>\n> <issue_description>### Workflow Failure\n> \n> **Workflow:** [Daily Test Improver](https://github.com/githubnext/agentics/tree/b466f28f0f65b68d6f2b10b15b44f51d787b93be/workflows/daily-test-improver.md)  \n> **Branch:** 13.3.rel1  \n> **Run:** https://github.com/grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22751229687\n> \n> \n> **⚠️ Code Push Failed**: A code push safe output failed, and subsequent safe outputs were cancelled.\n> **Code Push Errors:**\n> - `create_pull_request`: Failed to apply patch\n> \n> \n> \n> ### Action Required\n> \n> **Option 1: Assign this issue to Copilot**\n> \n> Assign this issue to Copilot using the `agentic-workflows` sub-agent to automatically debug and fix the workflow failure.\n> \n> **Option 2: Manually invoke the agent**\n> \n> Debug this workflow failure using your favorite Agent CLI and the `agentic-workflows` prompt.\n> \n> - Start your agent\n> - Load the `agentic-workflows` prompt from `.github/agents/agentic-workflows.agent.md` or <https://github.com/gi