https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions"},{"login":"grahame-white","id":214149191,"node_id":"U_kgDODMOoRw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214149191?v=4","html_url":"https://github.com/grahame-white","gravatar_id":"","type":"User","site_admin":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/events{/privacy}","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/following{/other_user}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/followers","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/gists{/gist_id}","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/repos","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/subscriptions"}],"node_id":"PR_kwDORdWri87Ibb5K","draft":false},{"id":4031418728,"number":153,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"ci: add per-stage cache save/restore for binutils stage","body":"## Description\n\nAdds the first per-stage `actions/cache` restore→build→save triple for the binutils stage (III-0) in `build-toolchain.yml`, establishing the pattern for subsequent stages.\n\n**`.github/workflows/build-toolchain.yml`:**\n- **`Restore cache – binutils`** — `actions/cache/restore` keyed on `stage-hashes.outputs.binutils` (the cascading hash from the existing \"Compute stage source hashes\" step)\n- **`Build stage – binutils`** — runs only on cache miss; uses `--skip_stages=gcc-first,newlib,newlib-nano,gcc-final,gcc-size-libstdcxx,gdb` to isolate the binutils build\n- **`Save cache – binutils`** — `actions/cache/save` with the same key; guarded by the same cache-miss condition\n\nAll three steps are inserted between \"Compute stage source hashes\" and the existing monolithic \"Cache toolchain build\" step. The monolithic cache is left in place; both coexist until all stages have per-stage caches. Same `actions/cache` SHA (`cdf6c1fa76f9f475f3d7449005a359c84ca0f306` / v5.0.3) as the rest of the workflow.\n\n**`build-toolchain.sh`** (bug fixes required by the new CI step): When `--skip_stages` is used to build only binutils, several post-build stages unconditionally attempted to access GCC-specific paths and binaries that do not exist in a binutils-only install. Fixed by guarding these operations with existence checks:\n- **III-9** `strip_host_objects`: wrapped `find lib/gcc/arm-none-eabi/$GCC_VER/` in a `-d` directory existence check\n- **III-10** `strip_target_objects`: wrapped the `.a` and `.o` `find` calls against `lib/gcc/arm-none-eabi/$GCC_VER` in a `-d` directory existence check\n- **III-11** `specs`: wrapped `arm-none-eabi-gcc -print-multi-lib` in a `-x` executable existence check\n- **III-12** `package_tbz2`: replaced the static `tar` argument list with a loop that only includes subdirectories (`arm-none-eabi`, `bin`, `lib`, `share`) that actually exist under `install-native/`; `lib` is explicitly deleted after binutils (III-0) and is absent until `gcc-first` repopulates it\n\n## Testing\n\n- YAML syntax validated.\n- Logic verified against the stage hash computation and `build-toolchain.sh --skip_stages` valid values (`binutils|gcc-first|newlib|newlib-nano|gcc-final|gcc-size-libstdcxx|gdb`).\n- Shell unit tests pass (28/28) after `build-toolchain.sh` changes.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] The PR title follows the Conventional Commits format (see note below)\n- [x] Changes are documented where appropriate\n\n<!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT -->\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Original prompt</summary>\n\n> \n> ----\n> \n> *This section details on the original issue you should resolve*\n> \n> <issue_title>[plan] Add per-stage cache save/restore for binutils stage in build-toolchain.yml</issue_title>\n> <issue_description>## Objective\n> \n> Add a per-stage `actions/cache` restore→build→save triple to `.github/workflows/build-toolchain.yml` for the **`binutils` stage** (III-0). This is the first and simplest stage — establishing the pattern that will be repeated for all remaining stages.\n> \n> ## Context\n> \n> Issue grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#75 describes replacing the single monolithic `install-native` cache with 7 per-stage caches. Each stage stores a cumulative snapshot of `install-native/` so restoring stage N gives you everything stages 0…N wrote.\n> \n> This issue covers only the `binutils` stage. The monolithic cache is left in place for now (it is removed in a later issue after all stages are covered). The two caches coexist temporarily; the per-stage cache provides a fast path for binutils-only changes.\n> \n> Depends on:\n> - grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#73\n> - grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#74\n> \n> ## Approach\n> \n> In `.github/workflows/build-toolchain.yml`, between the prerequisites build step and the existing monolithic toolchain cache step, insert:\n> \n> ```yaml\n> # --- Stage: binutils ---\n> - name: Restore cache – binutils\n>   id: cache-binutils\n>   uses: actions/cache/restore@(SHA) # v4\n>   with:\n>     path: install-native\n>     key: ${{ runner.os }}-stage-v1-${{ steps.src-hashes.outputs.binutils }}\n> \n> - name: Build stage – binutils\n>   if: steps.cache-binutils.outputs.cache-hit != 'true' && steps.cache-toolchain.outputs.cache-hit != 'true'\n>   run: |\n>     export JOBS=$(nproc)\n>     ./build-toolchain.sh \\\n>       --skip_steps=mingw,mingw-gdb-with-python,gdb-with-python,manual,package_sources \\\n>       --skip_stages=gcc-first,newlib,newlib-nano,gcc-final,gcc-size-libstdcxx,gdb\n> \n> - name: Save cache – binutils\n>   if: steps.cache-binutils.outputs.cache-hit != 'true' && steps.cache-toolchain.outputs.cache-hit != 'true'\n>   uses: actions/cache/save@(SHA) # v4\n>   with:\n>     path: install-native\n>     key: ${{ runner.os }}-stage-v1-${{ steps.src-hashes.outputs.binutils }}\n> ```\n> \n> Use the same `actions/cache` SHA already used in the file for the prerequisites cache.\n> \n> ## Files to Modify\n> \n> - `.github/workflows/build-toolchain.yml`\n> \n> ## Acceptance Criteria\n> \n> - [ ] A clean run saves the `binutils` cache after building only the binutils stage\n> - [ ] On a second run with unchanged `src/binutils/`, the `binutils` restore step hits and the Build stage – binutils step is skipped\n> - [ ] If only `src/gdb/` changes (not `src/binutils/`), the `binutils` cache still hits (cascade hash is unchanged)\n> - [ ] If `src/binutils/` changes, the `binutils` cache misses and rebuilds\n> - [ ] YAML is valid, workflow lints cleanly\n> \n> ## Notes\n> \n> This issue intentionally keeps the monolithic cache; both coexist. The monolithic cache is removed in a later issue once all stages have their own cache entries.\n> Related to grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#75, which is related to grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#71.\n> Related to grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#75\n> \n> \n> \n> \n> > Generated by [Plan Command](https://github.com/grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22737048557) for issue grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#75 · [◷](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Agrahame-white%2Fgnu-tools-for-stm32+is%3Aissue+%22gh-aw-workflow-call-id%3A+grahame-white%2Fgnu-tools-for-stm32%2Fplan%22+in%3Abody)\n> >\n> > To install this [agentic workflow](https://github.com/github/gh-aw/tree/852cb06ad52958b402ed982b69957ffc57ca0619/.github/workflows/plan.md), run\n> > ```\n> > gh aw add github/gh-aw/.github/workflows/plan.md@852cb06ad52958b402ed982b69957ffc57ca0619\n> > ```\n> > - [ ] expires <!-- gh-aw-expires: 2026-03-07T21:24:20.808Z --> on Mar 7, 2026, 9:24 PM UTC\n> \n> <!-- gh-aw-agentic-workflow: Plan Command, engine: copilot, id: 22737048557, workflow_id: plan, run: https://github.com/grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22737048557 -->\n> \n> <!-- gh-aw-workflow-id: plan -->\n> <!-- gh-aw-workflow-call-id: grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/plan --></issue_description>\n> \n> ## Comments on the Issue (you are @copilot in this section)\n> \n> <comments>\n> </comments>\n> \n\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX -->\n\n- Fixes grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#141\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS -->\n---\n\n💬 We'd love your input! Share your thoughts on Copilot coding agent in our [2 minute survey](https://gh.io/copilot-coding-agent-survey).\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","user":{"login":"Copilot","id":198982749,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","site_admin":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions"},"comments":4,"closed_at":"2026-03-06T07:21:25Z","created_at":"2026-03-06T00:21:51Z","updated_at":"2026-03-06T07:21:28Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/153","html_url":"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/153","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/153/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/153/events","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/153/labels{/name}","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32","pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pulls/153","html_url":"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/153","diff_url":"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/153.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/153.patch","merged_at":"2026-03-06T07:21:25Z"},"reactions":{"total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/153/reactions"},"assignees":[{"login":"Copilot","id":198982749,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","site_admin":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions"},{"login":"grahame-white","id":214149191,"node_id":"U_kgDODMOoRw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214149191?v=4","html_url":"https://github.com/grahame-white","gravatar_id":"","type":"User","site_admin":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/events{/privacy}","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/following{/other_user}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/followers","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/gists{/gist_id}","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/repos","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/subscriptions"}],"node_id":"PR_kwDORdWri87IW_f2","draft":false},{"id":4030831436,"number":148,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"test: add shell unit tests for build-toolchain.sh argument parsing","body":"## Description\n\nThe argument-parsing logic in `build-toolchain.sh` (covering `--skip_steps`, `--build_type`, `--skip_stages`, `--with-multilib-list`, and related flags) was untested and unsourceable without triggering a full toolchain build.\n\n**`build-toolchain-args.sh`** (new) — extracts argument parsing into a sourceable helper:\n- `_toolchain_usage()` — usage text documenting all supported flags including `--skip_stages`\n- `parse_toolchain_args()` — sets all defaults and parses/validates all flags using safe bash parameter expansion (no `echo | sed`); supports `--skip_steps`, `--skip_stages`, `--build_type`, and `--with-multilib-list`\n\n**`build-toolchain.sh`** — replaces the inline parsing block with:\n```bash\n. \"$script_path/build-toolchain-args.sh\"\nparse_toolchain_args \"$@\"\n```\nAlso fixes a merge conflict where the `--skip_stages` validation block was calling the now-removed `usage` function; changed to `_toolchain_usage`.\n\n**`tests/test-build-toolchain-args.sh`** (new) — 59 test cases across 7 groups using the same plain-bash harness as `test-build-common.sh`:\n- `--skip_steps` — all valid step names, comma→space conversion\n- `--skip_stages` — all valid stage names, comma→space conversion\n- `--build_type` — `native`, `ppa`, `debug`, combinations\n- Defaults when no flags given (including `skip_stages`)\n- `--with-multilib-list` parsing\n- Multiple flags combined (including all 4 flags together)\n- Error exits for unrecognised flag, bad `--build_type`, bad `--skip_steps`\n\n**`.github/workflows/shell-unit-tests.yml`** — runs both test scripts; adds `build-toolchain.sh` and `build-toolchain-args.sh` to the paths-filter.\n\n## Testing\n\n```\nbash tests/test-build-common.sh              # 28 passed, 0 failed (unchanged)\nbash tests/test-build-toolchain-args.sh      # 59 passed, 0 failed\n```\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] The PR title follows the Conventional Commits format (see note below)\n- [x] Changes are documented where appropriate\n\n---\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **PR title must follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) format.**\n>\n> PRs are squashed into the target branch using the **PR title** as the commit message.\n> The PR title must therefore conform to commitlint requirements:\n>\n> ```\n> <type>[(optional scope)][!]: <description>\n> ```\n>\n> Common types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `chore`, `refactor`, `test`, `ci`, `build`, `perf`, `style`, `revert`\n>\n> Examples: `feat: add ARMv8-M support`, `fix: correct stack calculation`, `docs: update build instructions`\n>\n> Individual commits **within** the PR do **not** need to follow this format.\n\n<!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT -->\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Original prompt</summary>\n\n> \n> ----\n> \n> *This section details on the original issue you should resolve*\n> \n> <issue_title>[plan] Add bats-core unit tests for build-toolchain.sh argument parsing</issue_title>\n> <issue_description>## Objective\n> \n> Add bats-core unit tests for the argument parsing logic in `build-toolchain.sh`, covering `--skip_steps`, `--build_type`, `--skip_stages`, and related flags.\n> \n> ## Background\n> \n> Issue grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#108 (Test Improver monthly activity) identified shell script unit testing as Priority 2. The argument parsing in `build-toolchain.sh` (~lines 85–155) handles multiple flags with complex semantics:\n> - `--skip_steps=STEPS` — comma-separated list converted to space-separated string\n> - `--build_type=` — controls native/mingw32/mingw-w64 builds\n> - `--skip_stages=` — controls which toolchain stages to skip\n> - Various boolean flags (`--ppa`, `--no-ppa`, etc.)\n> \n> This parsing is untested and failures could produce hard-to-debug broken builds.\n> \n> ## Prerequisites\n> \n> This issue depends on the bats-core setup established in the `saveenv`/`restoreenv` test issue. If bats-core is not yet added to the repo, follow the same approach chosen there.\n> \n> ## Approach\n> \n> 1. Isolate the argument-parsing logic for testing. The challenge is that `build-toolchain.sh` runs the full build when sourced. Options:\n>    - Extract argument-parsing into a separate sourceable function/file (preferred, small refactor)\n>    - Use `set -- (args)` and source only up to the argument parsing section with an early-exit guard\n> 2. Create `test/build-toolchain-args.bats` with test cases:\n>    - `--skip_steps=binutils,gcc` → `skip_steps` variable is `\"binutils gcc\"`\n>    - `--skip_steps=` (empty) → `skip_steps` is empty\n>    - `--build_type=mingw32` → `build_type` is set correctly\n>    - `--skip_stages=III` → `skip_stages` is set correctly\n>    - Unrecognised flag produces an error/usage message\n>    - Multiple flags can be combined\n> 3. Document how to run the tests.\n> \n> ## Files to Create / Modify\n> \n> - Create: `test/build-toolchain-args.bats`\n> - Modify: `build-toolchain.sh` (minimally, if extraction/guard is needed)\n> \n> ## Acceptance Criteria\n> \n> - [ ] At least 6 test cases covering argument parsing scenarios\n> - [ ] Tests do not trigger an actual toolchain build when run\n> - [ ] All tests pass on current `build-toolchain.sh`\n> - [ ] Tests are runnable locally with a single command\n> Related to grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#108\n> \n> \n> \n> \n> > Generated by [Plan Command](https://github.com/grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22697787836) for issue grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#108 · [◷](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Agrahame-white%2Fgnu-tools-for-stm32+is%3Aissue+%22gh-aw-workflow-call-id%3A+grahame-white%2Fgnu-tools-for-stm32%2Fplan%22+in%3Abody)\n> >\n> > To install this [agentic workflow](https://github.com/github/gh-aw/tree/852cb06ad52958b402ed982b69957ffc57ca0619/.github/workflows/plan.md), run\n> > ```\n> > gh aw add github/gh-aw/.github/workflows/plan.md@852cb06ad52958b402ed982b69957ffc57ca0619\n> > ```\n> > - [x] expires <!-- gh-aw-expires: 2026-03-07T01:31:10.104Z --> on Mar 7, 2026, 1:31 AM UTC\n> \n> <!-- gh-aw-agentic-workflow: Plan Command, engine: copilot, id: 22697787836, workflow_id: plan, run: https://github.com/grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22697787836 -->\n> \n> <!-- gh-aw-workflow-id: plan -->\n> <!-- gh-aw-workflow-call-id: grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/plan --></issue_description>\n> \n> <agent_instructions>Before starting to implement this issue first consider if the exisiting shell unit tests approach will be suitable for use with `build-toolchain.sh`.</agent_instructions>\n> \n> ## Comments on the Issue (you are @copilot in this section)\n> \n> <comments>\n> </comments>\n> \n\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX -->\n\n- Fixes grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#117\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS -->\n---\n\n🔒 GitHub Advanced Security automatically protects Copilot coding agent pull requests. You can protect all pull requests by enabling Advanced Security for your repositories. [Learn more about Advanced Security.](https://gh.io/cca-advanced-security)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","user":{"login":"Copilot","id":198982749,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubuser