actions"},"assignees":[{"login":"Copilot","id":198982749,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","site_admin":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions"},{"login":"grahame-white","id":214149191,"node_id":"U_kgDODMOoRw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214149191?v=4","html_url":"https://github.com/grahame-white","gravatar_id":"","type":"User","site_admin":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/events{/privacy}","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/following{/other_user}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/followers","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/gists{/gist_id}","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/repos","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/subscriptions"}],"node_id":"PR_kwDORdWri87IVYAb","draft":false},{"id":4030566400,"number":138,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"ci: add per-stage cascade cache key computation","body":"Adds a `stage-hashes` step to `build-toolchain.yml` that computes deterministic, cascading cache keys for each native build stage using `git rev-parse HEAD:<dir>` (O(1) tree-SHA lookup) instead of `hashFiles()` glob scanning the ~217k-file `src/` tree.\n\n### Key design\n\n- Each stage key hashes its own source directory SHA **chained to the prior stage's key**, giving cascade invalidation:\n  - `src/binutils` change → invalidates `binutils` + all downstream keys\n  - `src/gdb` change → invalidates only `gdb` + `final`\n- `scripts_hash` captures `build-toolchain.sh` + `build-common.sh` so build-script changes invalidate all stages\n- `prereqs_key` from the prerequisites cache step is included so prerequisite changes cascade through all stages\n\n### Outputs (via `${{ steps.stage-hashes.outputs.<name> }}`)\n\n`binutils` → `gcc-first` → `newlib` → `newlib-nano` → `gcc-final` → `gcc-size-libstdcxx` → `gdb` → `final`\n\nThese outputs are ready to be consumed by per-stage cache steps in subsequent work.\n\n## Testing\n\nStep logic validated via code review and CodeQL scan (0 alerts). Cascade invalidation properties verified by inspection of the key construction chain.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] The PR title follows the Conventional Commits format (see note below)\n- [x] Changes are documented where appropriate\n\n<!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT -->\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Original prompt</summary>\n\n\n----\n\n*This section details on the original issue you should resolve*\n\n<issue_title>[plan] Add cascade cache key computation step to build-toolchain.yml</issue_title>\n<issue_description>## Objective\n\nAdd a workflow step that computes a per-stage source-tree hash for each native build stage using `git rev-parse HEAD:(dir) | sha256sum` (not `hashFiles`). These hashes feed into the cascade cache keys added in subsequent issues.\n\n## Context\n\nThe current single-toolchain cache key uses `hashFiles('src/binutils/**', 'src/gcc/**', ...)` on multiple large directories. On the ~217 k-file `src/` tree this can time out. The fix (consistent with the existing prerequisites cache pattern) is to use `git rev-parse HEAD:(dir)` which returns the tree object SHA instantly without walking all files.\n\nFor cascade invalidation each stage's cache key must include the source hash of that stage **and** the cache key of all prior stages. A cache key is just a string, so it can be computed incrementally with shell string concatenation and sha256sum.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd a single new step **\"Compute stage source hashes\"** in `.github/workflows/build-toolchain.yml`, placed after the prerequisites cache step and before the toolchain build step:\n\n```yaml\n- name: Compute stage source hashes\n  id: stage-hashes\n  run: |\n    hash_dir() { git rev-parse HEAD:\"$1\" 2>/dev/null || echo \"missing-$1\"; }\n    scripts_hash=$(echo \"$(hash_dir build-toolchain.sh)$(hash_dir build-common.sh)\" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)\n    prereqs_key=\"${{ steps.cache-prerequisites.outputs.cache-primary-key }}\"\n\n    binutils_src=$(hash_dir src/binutils)\n    gcc_src=$(hash_dir src/gcc)\n    newlib_src=$(hash_dir src/newlib)\n    gdb_src=$(hash_dir src/gdb)\n    specs_src=$(hash_dir src/specs)\n\n    key_binutils=$(printf '%s' \"${{ runner.os }}-stage-binutils-${scripts_hash}-${prereqs_key}-${binutils_src}\" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)\n    key_gcc_first=$(printf '%s' \"${{ runner.os }}-stage-gcc-first-${scripts_hash}-${key_binutils}-${gcc_src}\" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)\n    key_newlib=$(printf '%s' \"${{ runner.os }}-stage-newlib-${scripts_hash}-${key_gcc_first}-${newlib_src}\" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)\n    key_newlib_nano=$(printf '%s' \"${{ runner.os }}-stage-newlib-nano-${scripts_hash}-${key_newlib}-${newlib_src}\" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)\n    key_gcc_final=$(printf '%s' \"${{ runner.os }}-stage-gcc-final-${scripts_hash}-${key_newlib_nano}-${gcc_src}\" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)\n    key_gcc_size=$(printf '%s' \"${{ runner.os }}-stage-gcc-size-libstdcxx-${scripts_hash}-${key_gcc_final}-${gcc_src}\" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)\n    key_gdb=$(printf '%s' \"${{ runner.os }}-stage-gdb-${scripts_hash}-${key_gcc_size}-${gdb_src}\" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)\n    key_final=$(printf '%s' \"${{ runner.os }}-stage-final-${scripts_hash}-${key_gdb}-${specs_src}\" | sha256sum | cut -d' ' -f1)\n\n    {\n      echo \"binutils=${key_binutils}\"\n      echo \"gcc-first=${key_gcc_first}\"\n      echo \"newlib=${key_newlib}\"\n      echo \"newlib-nano=${key_newlib_nano}\"\n      echo \"gcc-final=${key_gcc_final}\"\n      echo \"gcc-size-libstdcxx=${key_gcc_size}\"\n      echo \"gdb=${key_gdb}\"\n      echo \"final=${key_final}\"\n    } >> \"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n```\n\nThese outputs are then referenced as `${{ steps.stage-hashes.outputs.binutils }}` etc. by the per-stage cache steps (see the next sub-issue).\n\n## Files to Modify\n\n- `.github/workflows/build-toolchain.yml`\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The step runs in under 5 seconds (git tree-SHA lookup is O(1))\n- [ ] Each output key is a deterministic hash string\n- [ ] Changing `src/binutils/` changes the `binutils` key AND all downstream keys (gcc-first, newlib, ..., final)\n- [ ] Changing `src/gdb/` only changes the `gdb` and `final` keys\n- [ ] No `hashFiles()` calls on large `src/**` globs are introduced\n\n## Notes\n\nRelated to grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#71. PR title convention: `ci: add per-stage cascade cache key computation`.\nRelated to grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#71\n\n\n\n\n> Generated by [Plan Command](https://github.com/grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22666393924) for issue grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#71 · [◷](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Agrahame-white%2Fgnu-tools-for-stm32+is%3Aissue+%22gh-aw-workflow-call-id%3A+grahame-white%2Fgnu-tools-for-stm32%2Fplan%22+in%3Abody)\n>\n> To install this [agentic workflow](https://github.com/github/gh-aw/tree/852cb06ad52958b402ed982b69957ffc57ca0619/.github/workflows/plan.md), run\n> ```\n> gh aw add github/gh-aw/.github/workflows/plan.md@852cb06ad52958b402ed982b69957ffc57ca0619\n> ```\n> - [x] expires <!-- gh-aw-expires: 2026-03-06T11:06:20.421Z --> on Mar 6, 2026, 11:06 AM UTC\n\n<!-- gh-aw-agentic-workflow: Plan Command, engine: copilot, id: 22666393924, workflow_id: plan, run: https://github.com/grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22666393924 -->\n\n<!-- gh-aw-workflow-id: plan -->\n<!-- gh-aw-workflow-call-id: grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/plan --></issue_description>\n\n## Comments on the Is...\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX -->\n\n- Fixes grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#74\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS -->\n---\n\n💡 You can make Copilot smarter by setting up custom instructions, customizing its development environment and configuring Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers. Learn more [Copilot coding agent tips](https://gh.io/copilot-coding-agent-tips) in the docs.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","user":{"login":"Copilot","id":198982749,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","site_admin":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions"},"comments":0,"closed_at":"2026-03-06T00:20:25Z","created_at":"2026-03-05T20:56:22Z","updated_at":"2026-03-06T00:20:26Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/138","html_url":"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/138","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/138/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/138/events","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/138/labels{/name}","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32","pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pulls/138","html_url":"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/138","diff_url":"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/138.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/pull/138.patch","merged_at":"2026-03-06T00:20:24Z"},"reactions":{"total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/grahame-org/gnu-tools-for-stm32/issues/138/reactions"},"assignees":[{"login":"Copilot","id":198982749,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent","gravatar_id":"","type":"Bot","site_admin":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions"},{"login":"grahame-white","id":214149191,"node_id":"U_kgDODMOoRw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/214149191?v=4","html_url":"https://github.com/grahame-white","gravatar_id":"","type":"User","site_admin":false,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/events{/privacy}","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/following{/other_user}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/followers","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/gists{/gist_id}","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/repos","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/subscriptions"}],"node_id":"PR_kwDORdWri87IUlhf","draft":false},{"id":4030472477,"number":137,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"ci: add .shellcheckrc and targeted suppressions for legacy-style shellcheck findings","body":"~500 shellcheck findings across the three build scripts were all legacy-style noise, making it impossible to add shellcheck to CI without drowning real issues. This PR reduces warnings/errors to zero while fixing one real bug.\n\n## Changes\n\n### `.shellcheckrc` (new)\n- `shell=bash` — eliminates SC2148 (missing shebang) on sourced scripts\n- `disable=SC2034,SC2268,SC2016` — globally suppresses intentional patterns:\n  - `SC2034`: env-var constants in `build-common.sh` are consumed by sourcing scripts\n  - `SC2268`: historic `[ \"x$v\" = \"x\" ]` POSIX idiom, cosmetic-only churn to change\n  - `SC2016`: deferred `$` expansion inside `eval` strings\n\n### Real bug fixed — SC2145 (`build-toolchain.sh`)\n`${invalid[@]/#/\\\\n}` inside a double-quoted string mixes array elements with surrounding text as separate arguments. Changed to `${invalid[*]/#/\\\\n}`.\n\n### SC2155 fixed (`build-common.sh`)\nSplit `local dir=$(...)` / `local tmp=$(...)` into separate declare/assign so `dirname`/`mktemp` non-zero exit codes are not masked by `local`'s always-zero exit.\n\n### Targeted inline suppressions\n| Code | Count | Location | Rationale |\n|------|-------|----------|-----------|\n| SC1083 | 14 | `build-common.sh` `saveenvvar`/`restoreenv` | Intentional `eval \\${}` dynamic-variable pattern |\n| SC2154 | 7 | `build-common.sh`, `build-toolchain.sh` | Variables assigned via `eval`; shellcheck can't trace |\n| SC2046 | 5 | all three scripts | `$(dirname …)` / `$(basename …)` on controlled build paths |\n| SC2207 | 1 | `build-common.sh` | Word-split array population intentional |\n| SC2206 | 1 | `build-toolchain.sh` | Loop variable word-split intentional |\n| SC2038 | 1 | `build-toolchain.sh` | macOS-only `find \\| xargs file` pipeline |\n\n## Testing\n\n- `shellcheck --severity=warning` exits 0 with **0 warnings/errors** (down from 32; target ≤ 30)\n- `bash -n` syntax check passes on all three scripts\n- All 28 `tests/test-build-common.sh` unit tests pass\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] The PR title follows the Conventional Commits format (see note below)\n- [x] Changes are documented where appropriate\n\n<!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT -->\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Original prompt</summary>\n\n> \n> ----\n> \n> *This section details on the original issue you should resolve*\n> \n> <issue_title>[plan] Add .shellcheckrc and targeted suppressions for legacy-style findings in build scripts</issue_title>\n> <issue_description>## Objective\n> \n> Add a `.shellcheckrc` configuration file and targeted inline `# shellcheck disable=` comments to suppress the ~500 legacy-style findings in the three build scripts, so that shellcheck can be added to CI without noise drowning real issues.\n> \n> ## Background\n> \n> Issue grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#108 (Test Improver monthly activity) identified ~514 shellcheck findings across `build-common.sh`, `build-toolchain.sh`, `build-prerequisites.sh`. After fixing the 2 real SC2145 errors (separate issue), the remaining findings are legacy style:\n> \n> | Code   | Count | Description                                      | Category        |\n> |--------|-------|--------------------------------------------------|-----------------|\n> | SC2086 | 548   | Double-quote to prevent word splitting           | Legacy style    |\n> | SC2034 |  50   | Variable assigned but never used                 | Often intentional in envvar-save scripts |\n> | SC2102 |  21   | Ranges only match single chars in bracket exprs  | Legacy pattern  |\n> | SC2268 |  18   | Unnecessary `x`-prefix comparison (`[ \"x$v\" ...`) | Legacy shell idiom |\n> | SC1083 |  15   | Literal `{` or `}` outside arithmetic            | Quoting legacy  |\n> | SC2006 |  11   | Use `$(...)` notation instead of backticks       | Style           |\n> | SC2154 |   7   | Variable referenced but not assigned              | Often dynamic eval |\n> | SC2046 |   5   | Quote word-split in command substitution          | Legacy style    |\n> | SC2148 |   2   | No shebang (sourced scripts)                     | Not applicable  |\n> | SC2016 |   2   | Single-quoted `$` expansion                     | Intentional     |\n> \n> ## Approach\n> \n> 1. Add a `.shellcheckrc` at the repo root to set:\n>    - `shell=bash` (avoids SC2148 on sourced scripts)\n>    - Disable repo-wide legacy codes: `disable=SC2034,SC2268,SC2016`\n> 2. For `SC2086` (unquoted variables): These scripts intentionally use word-splitting on paths — add per-file or per-region `# shellcheck disable=SC2086` where intentional, rather than a global suppression. Focus on the most common patterns.\n> 3. For `SC2006` (backticks): These can be mechanically fixed with `sed`. Replace `` `expr ...` `` with `$(expr ...)` throughout.\n> 4. For `SC1083`, `SC2046`, `SC2102`, `SC2154`, `SC2162`, `SC2155`: add targeted inline suppressions only where the pattern is intentional.\n> 5. After changes, run `shellcheck build-common.sh build-toolchain.sh build-prerequisites.sh` and confirm finding count drops significantly.\n> \n> ## Files to Create / Modify\n> \n> - Create: `.shellcheckrc`\n> - Modify: `build-common.sh`, `build-toolchain.sh`, `build-prerequisites.sh` (inline suppressions where needed)\n> \n> ## Acceptance Criteria\n> \n> - [ ] `.shellcheckrc` exists and sets `shell=bash`\n> - [ ] `shellcheck` finding count drops to ≤ 30 (warnings/errors only, not style)\n> - [ ] No real bugs are suppressed — each suppression targets a demonstrably intentional pattern\n> - [ ] `bash -n` syntax check still passes on all three scripts\n> Related to grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#108\n> \n> \n> \n> \n> > Generated by [Plan Command](https://github.com/grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22697787836) for issue grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#108 · [◷](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Agrahame-white%2Fgnu-tools-for-stm32+is%3Aissue+%22gh-aw-workflow-call-id%3A+grahame-white%2Fgnu-tools-for-stm32%2Fplan%22+in%3Abody)\n> >\n> > To install this [agentic workflow](https://github.com/github/gh-aw/tree/852cb06ad52958b402ed982b69957ffc57ca0619/.github/workflows/plan.md), run\n> > ```\n> > gh aw add github/gh-aw/.github/workflows/plan.md@852cb06ad52958b402ed982b69957ffc57ca0619\n> > ```\n> > - [ ] expires <!-- gh-aw-expires: 2026-03-07T01:31:06.583Z --> on Mar 7, 2026, 1:31 AM UTC\n> \n> <!-- gh-aw-agentic-workflow: Plan Command, engine: copilot, id: 22697787836, workflow_id: plan, run: https://github.com/grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22697787836 -->\n> \n> <!-- gh-aw-workflow-id: plan -->\n> <!-- gh-aw-workflow-call-id: grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/plan --></issue_description>\n> \n> ## Comments on the Issue (you are @copilot in this section)\n> \n> <commen