events{/privacy}","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/following{/other_user}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/followers","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/gists{/gist_id}","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/repos","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/grahame-white/subscriptions"}],"node_id":"PR_kwDORdWri87IUSL0","draft":false},{"id":4030233313,"number":123,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix: replace $@ with $* in error/warning functions to fix SC2145","body":"## Description\n\n`$@` inside a double-quoted string with surrounding text (e.g. `\"$0: error: $@\"`) silently drops all arguments after the first. `$*` joins all arguments with IFS into a single string — the correct behaviour for message-formatting functions.\n\n- **`build-common.sh` lines ~30 and ~37**: `\"$0: error: $@\"` → `\"$0: error: $*\"` and `\"$0: warning: $@\"` → `\"$0: warning: $*\"`\n- **`build-common.sh` `error()` function**: Removed unreachable `set -u` that appeared after `exit 1`.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `shellcheck build-common.sh` — no SC2145 findings remain\n- `bash -n build-common.sh build-toolchain.sh build-prerequisites.sh` — syntax check passes\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] The PR title follows the Conventional Commits format (see note below)\n- [x] Changes are documented where appropriate\n\n---\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **PR title must follow [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) format.**\n>\n> PRs are squashed into the target branch using the **PR title** as the commit message.\n> The PR title must therefore conform to commitlint requirements:\n>\n> ```\n> <type>[(optional scope)][!]: <description>\n> ```\n>\n> Common types: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `chore`, `refactor`, `test`, `ci`, `build`, `perf`, `style`, `revert`\n>\n> Examples: `feat: add ARMv8-M support`, `fix: correct stack calculation`, `docs: update build instructions`\n>\n> Individual commits **within** the PR do **not** need to follow this format.\n\n<!-- START COPILOT ORIGINAL PROMPT -->\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Original prompt</summary>\n\n> \n> ----\n> \n> *This section details on the original issue you should resolve*\n> \n> <issue_title>[plan] Fix SC2145 shellcheck errors in build-common.sh (error/warning functions)</issue_title>\n> <issue_description>## Objective\n> \n> Fix the two confirmed `(error)` severity shellcheck findings in `build-common.sh`. These represent genuine bugs, not legacy style issues.\n> \n> ## Background\n> \n> Running `shellcheck build-common.sh` reports:\n> \n> ```\n> In build-common.sh line 30:\n>     echo \"$0: error: $@\" >&2\n>                      ^-- SC2145 (error): Argument mixes string and array. Use * or separate argument.\n> \n> In build-common.sh line 37:\n>     echo \"$0: warning: $@\" >&2\n>                        ^-- SC2145 (error): Argument mixes string and array. Use * or separate argument.\n> ```\n> \n> `$@` inside a double-quoted string with other text produces a single concatenated word for the first argument only, losing the rest. Using `\"$*\"` or `\"$@\"` standalone (with proper quoting) is the correct fix.\n> \n> ## Approach\n> \n> 1. In `build-common.sh`, locate the `error()` function (~line 30) and `warning()` function (~line 37).\n> 2. Change `\"$0: error: $@\"` → `\"$0: error: $*\"` (and same for warning).  \n>    `$*` joins all arguments with IFS into a single string, which is the intended behaviour for these message-formatting functions.\n> 3. Run `shellcheck build-common.sh` to confirm the two errors are resolved.\n> 4. Verify the scripts still function correctly by running `bash -n build-common.sh build-toolchain.sh build-prerequisites.sh`.\n> \n> ## Files to Modify\n> \n> - `build-common.sh` — lines ~30 and ~37\n> \n> ## Acceptance Criteria\n> \n> - [ ] `shellcheck build-common.sh` reports zero `(error)` severity findings\n> - [ ] The `error()` and `warning()` functions still produce correct output (verified by manual inspection or a quick test)\n> - [ ] `bash -n` syntax check passes on all three scripts\n> Related to grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#108\n> \n> \n> \n> \n> > Generated by [Plan Command](https://github.com/grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22697787836) for issue grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#108 · [◷](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Agrahame-white%2Fgnu-tools-for-stm32+is%3Aissue+%22gh-aw-workflow-call-id%3A+grahame-white%2Fgnu-tools-for-stm32%2Fplan%22+in%3Abody)\n> >\n> > To install this [agentic workflow](https://github.com/github/gh-aw/tree/852cb06ad52958b402ed982b69957ffc57ca0619/.github/workflows/plan.md), run\n> > ```\n> > gh aw add github/gh-aw/.github/workflows/plan.md@852cb06ad52958b402ed982b69957ffc57ca0619\n> > ```\n> > - [x] expires <!-- gh-aw-expires: 2026-03-07T01:31:05.512Z --> on Mar 7, 2026, 1:31 AM UTC\n> \n> <!-- gh-aw-agentic-workflow: Plan Command, engine: copilot, id: 22697787836, workflow_id: plan, run: https://github.com/grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/actions/runs/22697787836 -->\n> \n> <!-- gh-aw-workflow-id: plan -->\n> <!-- gh-aw-workflow-call-id: grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32/plan --></issue_description>\n> \n> ## Comments on the Issue (you are @copilot in this section)\n> \n> <comments>\n> </comments>\n> \n\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX -->\n\n- Fixes grahame-white/gnu-tools-for-stm32#113\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS -->\n---\n\n💬 We'd love your input! Share your thoughts on Copilot coding agent in our [2 minute survey](https://gh.io/copilot-coding-agent-survey).\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","user":{"login":"Copilot","id":198982749,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.c